    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This dispute is decided on the cancellation-grace rule and the record's own arithmetic. Trip record EV-TRIP-00852 shows the ride was accepted at 18:10:00 and the rider cancelled at 18:11:30 — 90 seconds later. The platform policy in force for this trip sets platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec at 180 seconds, so the cancellation fell well inside the grace period. Under POL-NS-10(a) a rider's cancellation within that grace is not chargeable whatever the driver's position, and a driver's early arrival does not shorten it; under POL-NS-10(c) the cancellation fee charged on such a cancellation is refunded in full with no driver compensation. Fare breakdown EV-FARE-00852 records exactly one charge — the cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 (total_charged SGD 4.50, refund_issued_sgd SGD 0.00) — so the whole contested sum of SGD 4.50 is returned to the rider. The no-show route does not rescue the fee. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and fails at every limb: there is no driver 'arrived' event in EV-TRIP-00852 (limb (a)); the driver's track in EV-GPS-00852 places him 667.17 m from the pickup pin on all ten fixes, so there is no qualifying in-radius fix under POL-NS-02 (limb (b)); the qualifying in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period (limb (c), POL-NS-06); and the record shows cancelled_by RIDER with cancellation_reason_code null and no driver termination for no-show (limb (d)). The 667 m separation also puts the case outside POL-NS-03's 400 m wrong-entrance window, so no wrong-entrance analysis applies; the driver's advocate properly conceded he does not contend arrival. On the driver's points: the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against 100 completed trips over 30 days, far below the conjunctive 4-or-more AND above-0.08 test — but that only clears the way for a payout, it does not create one, because POL-NS-10(c) expressly awards no driver compensation on a grace-period cancellation. There is no false-arrival marker to refer, because the record contains no 'arrived' event, so POL-NS-05 is not engaged and its false-arrival referral does not arise. The rider's own message at 18:10:20 ('I selected the wrong destination and need to cancel') confirms the trip ended by her election; no conduct referral against the driver is supported and none is made. Confidence: the deciding facts (the 90-second interval and the SGD 4.50 charge) are carried by EV-TRIP-00852 and EV-FARE-00852, both at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes, so the cap is 1.0 and the finding is well above the 0.70 escalation floor; no POL-NS-09 trigger fires. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and executes automatically on issue, subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

