    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00852 is refunded in full, and the driver receives no compensation.\n\nThe governing fact is on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00852): the trip was accepted at 18:10:00 and the rider cancelled at 18:11:30, ninety seconds later. POL-NS-10(a) makes a rider's cancellation within the grace-after-matching period non-chargeable whatever the driver's position, and the grace in force for this trip is platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec = 180 seconds; a driver's early arrival does not shorten it. Ninety seconds is inside the grace, so POL-NS-10(c) requires the cancellation fee charged on that cancellation to be refunded in full with no driver compensation. The ledger (EV-FARE-00852) shows exactly one charge, a cancellation_fee of SGD 4.50, total_charged SGD 4.50 and refund_issued_sgd 0.00; there is no base, distance, time, surge, toll or waiting-time line in issue, so the whole contested sum is the cancellation fee and the whole of it is returned.\n\nThe driver's own evidence confirms the charge does not stand on performance either, and the driver rightly says so rather than stretching the point. On EV-GPS-00852 the driver's ten fixes sit 667.17 m from the pickup pin throughout and stationary, with qualifying_fix_count 0 and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0 seconds against the 180-second minimum; the trip record carries no 'arrived' event, no boarding event, cancellation_reason_code null and cancelled_by RIDER. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) through (d) are therefore not made out, POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 would each independently deny the fee, and the 667.17 m separation is far beyond POL-NS-03's 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling, so no wrong-entrance analysis applies. The driver also cannot be caught by POL-NS-05, because no arrival marker was ever recorded and there is no marker to be false; POL-NS-05 is not engaged and no false-arrival referral is made. The rider's limb (a), (c) and (d)